{"abstract":"The Danish government's plans to send prisoners to serve their sentences in Kosovo will not solve the overcrowding in Danish prisons. Instead, the plan reinforces a trend over the last 20 years where the judicial system increasingly marginalizes and imposes harsher sentences on individuals from so-called \"non-Western countries.\" This is a discriminatory penal practice and an unjust justice policy.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","Hansen, Nanna","Schultz, Veronika","Jefferson, Andrew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752583"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dansk leje af fængsel i kosovo cementerer en diskriminerende straffepraksis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.eftertrykket.dk/2024/02/21/dansk-leje-af-faengsel-i-kosovo-cementerer-en-diskriminerende-straffepraksis/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752583","ids":["au-08173151-3eb6-40ef-95c5-eb500c3d2ca6"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A031BDA9B8046A2540BD2DFD44AA817A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.eftertrykket.dk/2024/02/21/dansk-leje-af-faengsel-i-kosovo-cementerer-en-diskriminerende-straffepraksis/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Nanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","name":"Schultz, Veronika","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"jeffersonpau","last":"Jefferson","name":"Jefferson, Andrew","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["au-08173151-3eb6-40ef-95c5-eb500c3d2ca6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Dansk leje af fængsel i Kosovo cementerer en diskriminerende straffepraksis","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752583","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This article explores how feminist teachers can engage with affective pedagogies when teaching intersectional gender studies. In the context of global corporate universities that emphasise action plans on diversity, equality, and inclusion, and alongside a rise in anti-gender and anti-diversity politics both within society and on campuses, feminist scholars encounter challenges in navigating affective contestations and tensions when teaching intersectional gender studies. These tensions can both evoke uncomfortable atmospheres and offer hopeful glimpses of societal changes and solidarities. In addressing this, we employ the idiom of ‘the elephant in the room’ to exploring how affective tensions emerge in the classroom and how feminist teachers may respond to and care about them. Drawing on literature on affective pedagogies, we conceptualise affects as intensities that move within and infuse feminist classrooms and analytically unpack two experiences of elephants emerging when teaching an intersectional gender studies programme at a Danish university. Specifically, we offer two takes on affective pedagogies that we name ‘swaying the elephant’ and ‘holding the elephant’ and discuss the ways in which feminist teachers can nurture ethico-political and affirmative practices in education.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Vertelyté, Manté","Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","Khawaja, Iram","Plotnikof, Mie","Staunæs, Dorthe","Sandager, Jette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-727627"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caring about the elephants in feminist classrooms affective pedagogies in an intersectional gender studies program","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5117/TVGN2024.2-3.011.VERT","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-727627","ids":["au-70e8c7f5-a5a8-496f-8a39-8963a90a343c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CABF70E974EAE078535D3ABF6D7569EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/432482241/Caring_about_the_elephants_in_feminist_classrooms_-_Affective_pedagogies_in_an_intersectional_gender_studies_program.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5117/TVGN2024.2-3.011.VERT","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Education Studies, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Manté","key":"vertelytépau","last":"Vertelyté","locid":"780c8bc2-e8d7-46c0-914e-08197d820e50","name":"Vertelyté, Manté","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Iram","key":"khawajapau","last":"Khawaja","locid":"d5c034f8-2f3f-4e2d-ad31-f4169167546a","name":"Khawaja, Iram","orcid":"0000-0002-5231-8729","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mie","key":"plotnikofpau","last":"Plotnikof","locid":"a7e3ed42-bd7d-4ab4-9eca-bc3d99aac90a","name":"Plotnikof, Mie","orcid":"0000-0002-3670-3758","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorthe","key":"staunæspau","last":"Staunæs","locid":"b6de50a1-3b2c-4f12-89f8-ebf5a790d55a","name":"Staunæs, Dorthe","orcid":"0000-0002-6554-6632","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jette","key":"sandagerpau","last":"Sandager","locid":"0ef5471f-0d75-41a5-b428-096bc5d8cf3f","name":"Sandager, Jette","orcid":"0000-0001-5522-9652","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5117/tvgn2024.2-3.011.vert","issn":["23522437"],"issue":"2/3","journal":"Tijdschrift voor Genderstudies","pages":"265-285","publisher":"Amsterdam University Press","status":"p","title":"Tijdschrift voor Genderstudies","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70e8c7f5-a5a8-496f-8a39-8963a90a343c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Caring about the elephants in feminist classrooms : Affective pedagogies in an intersectional gender studies program","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-727627","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Realitydeltageren Teitur Skoubo blev i efteråret 2022 idømt to år og seks måneders fængsel i byretten for vold og voldtægt mod en unavngiven kvinde. Seks måneder senere var sagen i landsretten, og her blev realitydeltageren dømt for vold mod kvinden, men frifundet for voldtægten (Buhl & Mejborn 2022). Hvor parternes erfaringer af hændelsen forblev de samme, gik den tiltalte fra skyldig til ikke skyldig i rettens øjne. Vi lever i et samfund, hvor domstolene har magten til at afgøre sociale konflikter. Dommerne filtrerer hændelser gennem lovgivnings bestemmelser for at afgøre, hvorvidt det kan bevises, om en hændelse juridisk set er kriminel. Dommerne skal vurdere hvorvidt det kan antages, at den tiltalte “udenfor enhver rimelig tvivl” kan kendes skyldig, og ultimativt fængsles. Retten bestemmer officielt, hvad der er en juridisk gyldig vurdering, og ikke hvad der “rent faktisk skete” (Lynch 2011), alligevel får disse afgørelser en stor indflydelse på de socialt etablerede sandheder (Smart 1989:13). Retten har på denne vis en institutionel magt til at etablere en virkelighed (reality) om skyld og ansvar i samfundet (jf. Boltanski 2011). Ved at åbne døren til retssalen, vil vi give en nærværende skildring og analyse af, hvad en dom dækker over. Retten er ikke blot ét homogent hele (Smart 1989), og loven er ikke én aktør, der gør noget af sig selv (Latour 2010). Der er en række af praksisser, aktører, værdier, mv. på spil. Vi kan dog ikke ignorere den magt, som institutionen samlet set udøver; omend retten ikke eksisterer uden aktører til at repræsentere og opretholde den (Boltanski 2011). Derfor insisterer vi på at tale om rettens epistemologi, som en institutionel forståelsesramme opretholdt af rettens aktører.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","Jessing, Birke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-667934"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"når retten har overtaget konflikterne","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-667934","ids":["au-232e4383-7ed6-44b7-b5a9-148c37c9c058"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0194E94FB1B5EEB8B414EB49AE09E851"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Department of Educational Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Birke","key":"jessingpau","last":"Jessing","name":"Jessing, Birke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09043535"],"issue":"168","journal":"Social Kritik:Tidsskrift for social analyse & debat","pages":"52-61","publisher":"Selskabet til Fremme af Social Debat, Danmark","status":"p","title":"Social Kritik:Tidsskrift for social analyse & debat","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-232e4383-7ed6-44b7-b5a9-148c37c9c058"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Når retten har overtaget konflikterne","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-667934","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Psychologist Ida Koch has been a key figure in Danish prison activism from the 1970s to the present day. She was involved in, among other things, KRIM and the Isolation Group under \"Retspolitik Forening\" as well as engaging in a wide range of other prison critical contexts, both as an activist, psychologist, scholar, and much more. During two episodes, she shares stories about the prison-critical work she has taken part in stretching through half a century.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","Rasmussen, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718120"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interview med ida koch i ii","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.listennotes.com/podcasts/f%C3%A6ngselskritik-merethe-g-andreas-r-nLsOgCMPeA5/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718120","ids":["au-dfa7ef69-aa56-4cea-afc8-7e1d8e6ad1c9"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9F051A42DB9072705D6275518B4E1393"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.listennotes.com/podcasts/f%C3%A6ngselskritik-merethe-g-andreas-r-nLsOgCMPeA5/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingppu","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"rasmussenppu","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Andreas","rank":2,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dfa7ef69-aa56-4cea-afc8-7e1d8e6ad1c9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Interview med Ida Koch I+II","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718120","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"100 sentence increases in ten years have resulted in overcrowded prisons. Crime rate has not increased, but we lock people up for longer. It is not given that the current development must be answered with more prison cells and more prison officers. It is an expression of a crisis of justice, where we have become accustomed to the fact that crime must be dealt with through incarceration. The many prison sentence increases that have created the prison crisis can be phased out again. We can demand that the politicians work for an ambitious justice policy that actually solves the challenges. If we really want to solve the prison crisis, the solution is not more officers. The solution is fewer inmates and more justice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","Ahrensbøll Schultz, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-717765"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overfyldte fængsler kalder ikke på flere betjente men på et samfund med færre indsatte","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.information.dk/debat/2023/10/overfyldte-faengsler-kalder-paa-flere-betjente-paa-samfund-faerre-indsatte","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-717765","ids":["au-8dc17e2c-8a60-4281-96da-29c31afeb31b"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4768E9F517ACA2ED2309E05E7AE07B64"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Educational Psychology, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"ahrensbøllschultzpau","last":"Ahrensbøll Schultz","name":"Ahrensbøll Schultz, Veronika","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16022572"],"newspaper":"Information","publisher":"Dagbladet Information","status":"p","title":"Information"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8dc17e2c-8a60-4281-96da-29c31afeb31b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Overfyldte fængsler kalder ikke på flere betjente, men på et samfund med færre indsatte","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-717765","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Ønsket om hurtige politiske løsninger på lange ventelister og en presset ressourcesituation i landets PPR-enheder har i den aktuelle debat ført til, at forskellige interessentgrupper har argumenteret for en genetablering af uddannelsen til skolepsykolog (cand.pæd. i psykologi), som blev udbudt af Danmarks Pædagogiske Universitet (DPU) indtil 2004. Denne uddannelse blev, som konsekvens af kravet om 2-årige kandidatuddannelser, erstattet af kandidatuddannelsen i pædagogisk psykologi (cand.pæd. i pædagogisk psykologi), som også i dag fortrinsvis henvender sig til professionsbachelorer med lærer- eller pædagogbaggrund. De studerende på uddannelsen har fortrinsvis baggrund som professionsbachelor som lærer eller pædagog, og som færdige kandidater i pædagogisk psykologi indgår de med deres kombination af praksiserfaring fra skoler og dagtilbud og deres viden om pædagogisk psykologi i de tværfaglige PPR-teams. Et mindretal i Folketinget har imidlertid pålagt uddannelses- og forskningsministeren at iværksætte en sondering af behovet for en ny psykologfaglig efteruddannelse til lærere og pædagoger, der dog ikke skal lede til autorisation. DPU har derfor fundet anledning til at gennemføre en undersøgelse af PPR-lederes opfattelse af udfordringer og muligheder med bemanding, uddannelsesbehov, faggrænser og spørgsmålet om autorisation med henblik på at bidrage med opdateret viden om de mest centrale udfordringer.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-667814"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ppr i paradigmeskifte en undersøgelse af ppr lederes opfattelser af udfordringer og muligheder med bemanding uddannelsesbehov og faggrænser","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dpu.au.dk/fileadmin/edu/Udgivelser/Rapporter/PPR_i_paradigmeskifte_-_rapport.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-667814","ids":["au-0af79ed8-927c-42e0-a0ea-69c9ffa96d0b"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9171A9EC4FD6667CDCE0D72190CC2563"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dpu.au.dk/fileadmin/edu/Udgivelser/Rapporter/PPR_i_paradigmeskifte_-_rapport.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Department of Educational Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Aarhus Universitet"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0af79ed8-927c-42e0-a0ea-69c9ffa96d0b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"PPR i paradigmeskifte : En undersøgelse af PPR-lederes opfattelser af udfordringer og muligheder med bemanding, uddannelsesbehov og faggrænser","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-667814","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A feminist theorization around vulnerability and interdependence as primary human conditions is slowly emerging (Butler, 2020; Cavarero, 2011). The deep ontological realization of vulnerability is followed by a fragile but forceful ethics of non-violence, which challenges scholars who have moved to the need of new forms of governing to combat the fear/threat of vulnerability (Plato, Hobbes, Hegel). Vulnerability is however differently distributed and our ways to becoming autonomous beings can be disrupted. From this outset, how can we understand crime prevention and resocialization? My PhD project concerns women’s way to acts deemed criminal by the state, and their experiences with crime preventive initiatives throughout their life course. In a time where tougher punishments are a primary mode of addressing harm within politics, an ethics of non-violence may be a needed companion in thinking differently around cycles of harm. Perhaps harm is what we want to address, not merely crime.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-212291"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-19","place":"København, dk","start":"2022-08-18","title":"Dansk kønsforsknings indre og ydre rammer","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vulnerable crime harm prevention","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-212291","ids":["au-91851f50-2628-4f8c-b767-4a4af1c247df"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E481141DBC5C7BA865F86FF1826320C8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Department of Educational Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-91851f50-2628-4f8c-b767-4a4af1c247df"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Vulnerable crime harm prevention","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-212291","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Come the new semester, we as employees at ITU are expected to be returning to our offices after spending close to 1,5 years working from home, or at least under different restrictions of access to our workplace. During this time, the ETHOS Lab has taken the plants home, left our other non-human companions in the Lab, and have tried to continue to maintain community digitally. Now, we will repopulate the Lab and, although the joy of reunification is strong, so is the willful hesitance and resistance in returning to “normalcy”. What does it mean to return when conditions are still in flux? What do we return to when our work lives have become reconfigured into new “normals” sustained over many months?","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-183882"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"upon returning thinking transitioning through the lens of transformation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ethos.itu.dk/upon-returning-thinking-transitioning-through-the-lens-of-transformation/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-183882","ids":["au-5f919c2d-2070-4b51-aa68-b0b461fcd31d"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-52026F5A34875D57DBD199BDA5E23593"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ethos.itu.dk/upon-returning-thinking-transitioning-through-the-lens-of-transformation/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Department of Educational Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merethe Riggelsen","key":"gjørdingpau","last":"Gjørding","locid":"afb14d34-6c1e-4db2-b048-a16c5747a1ef","name":"Gjørding, Merethe Riggelsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["au-5f919c2d-2070-4b51-aa68-b0b461fcd31d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Upon Returning : Thinking Transitioning Through the Lens of Transformation","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-183882","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
